<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The structural connection through which the execution of a process operator is assigned to a technical resource."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://www.vdi.de/richtlinien/details/vdivde-3682-blatt-1-formalisierte-prozessbeschreibungen-konzept-und-grafische-darstellung> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasInput> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The chain reads: a flow leading to this operator originates from that state. Typed sub properties keep the inference from firing between two states or two operators."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#dependency> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Adopted from the VDI 3682 ODP of Helmut Schmidt University and not contained in the standard itself.\n\nUnder the open world assumption several inputs of one process operator always denote alternatives. Where inputs are required jointly, this has to be stated explicitly. The property acts as a conjunction between states, so that an expression such as \"A and B, or C and D\" becomes representable: dependency is asserted between A and B and between C and D.\n\nThe property complements ParallelFlow. A parallel flow qualifies a single connection, whereas dependency groups several connections into one conjunction."@en .
