<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Flow> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Figure 3 lists the flow as one of the eight symbols of the graphical notation, where it is an edge rather than an object.\n\nReifying the flow as a class is a design decision of this pattern and deviates from the VDI 3682 ODP of Helmut Schmidt University, which models flows as object properties. A reified flow can be identified, annotated and marked as parallel or alternative, none of which an edge can carry.\n\nThe direct properties hasInput and hasOutput are retained and inferred from the reified flows through property chains, so that reasoning over predecessor and successor is unaffected by the reification."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#isCharacterizedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates an object of the formalised process description to one of its characteristics."@en .
_:Naa26db91c29d4ca79c1f064c930a2808 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#isAssignedTo> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a process operator directly to the technical resource realising it. Inferred from the reified assignment, not modelled directly."@en .
