<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasStateSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasSource> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a process operator to an assignment describing which technical resource realises it."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#revisionNumber> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Things of the real world that are transformed within a technical process. The generic term also covers flows of materials and substances."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Ontology design pattern for the formalised description of technical processes according to VDI/VDE 3682 Part 1 (concept and graphic representation) and Part 2 (information model), issue May 2015.\n\nThe pattern covers the process network of states and process operators, the technical resources realising the operators, the system limit bounding the observation horizon, and the attribute structure of identification and characteristics.\n\nThe pattern is one of four subdomain patterns of the AIAS information model, which describes AI applications in automated plants together with the automated plant and the technical process. It is designed to be imported through owl:imports and aligned by way of the AIAS alignment ontology."@en .
_:Na03b618bc12340ab8eec167efc997c50 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
