<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasSubProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a process operator to the process describing its decomposition. Inferred, not modelled."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#isComposedOf> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.1. Only process operators may be decomposed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#longName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 2, Section 5.1."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Energy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Energy required or released by a process operator, for example electrical energy or heat. Energy occurs as input and as output of a process."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasSubProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Process> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasOutput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a process operator to a state leaving it. Inferred from the reified flows, not modelled directly."@en .
